infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title open() default encoding: the cross-host trap
  desc Same source line, different decoding per host — until you name the encoding
  compares
    - label Omit encoding= (locale default)
      children
        - label Mac / modern Linux: utf-8
          desc locale.getpreferredencoding() happens to be utf-8 here
        - label Windows: cp1252
          desc Different default — the same bytes decode to different chars
        - label Bare C-locale container: latin-1
          desc CI and containers often run a stripped C locale
        - label Same file decodes differently per host
          desc The works-on-my-Mac, breaks-in-CI class of bug
    - label Pass encoding='utf-8'
      children
        - label Decoding fixed, locale-independent
          desc The bytes-to-str mapping no longer depends on the machine
        - label José round-trips on every host
          desc Accented names survive instead of turning to garbage
        - label Same result on every host
          desc Laptop, Windows, CI, container all agree
        - label The unconditional one-line fix
          desc For text files, always name the encoding
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
